Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 03:55:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 6 part 2: agency subscriptions, client rebilling,
 invitations, onboarding, transfers, white-label sign-in

- Agencies subscribe to the platform through Stripe Billing (Checkout and
  the customer portal); a signed webhook is the only writer of subscription
  state. Agency plans limit client accounts; a lapsed subscription blocks new
  clients without disabling existing ones.
- Client rebilling: a monthly fee plus metered usage at the agency's rates,
  drafted as one invoice per client and month (on demand or automatically).
- Email invitations with hashed, expiring, single-use tokens; the accepting
  account's email must match; new people create their account from the link.
- Guided client setup: account, time zone, approved facts, plan, draft
  website and owner invitation in one pass.
- Account transfer between agencies with the receiving agency's acceptance
  and the client owner's consent.
- White-label console domains with branded sign-in and sidebar; verified
  website and console domains are added to Netlify automatically when
  NETLIFY_API_TOKEN and NETLIFY_SITE_ID are set.

